He moved between three Brighton defenders before catapulting himself to the free field.
Aguero then found himself encircled by four green jerseys.
He humiliated a defender before surpassing several others on the edge of the Brighton area.
He then made a passage to the left, where Sterling found it.
The English striker used the first touch in the area to return the ball to Aguero, who used his right foot to beat Brighton goalkeeper Mathew Ryan with a shot to the right.
“Aguero is having foot problems,” City coach Pep Guardiola told reporters.
"We talked about making him play 55, 60 minutes.
That's what happened.
We were lucky he managed to score at that time.”
But it was Sterling who initially brought the Sky Blues ahead in the fight for the Premier League.
The goal came in the 29th minute.
Aguero received the ball deep on Brighton's field.
He sent a nice filter ball along his left flank to Leroy Sane.
Sane took a few steps before driving Sterling towards the second post.
The Sky Blues striker pulled the ball into the net just before coming off the field.
City will campaign against Hoffenheim in the Champions-League group at 12:55 p.m. on Tuesday at the Rhein-Neckar-Arena stadium in Sinsheim in Germany.
