They said, ‘Don’t go out with that cap on.’
They bullied me!
And so they told me I’m an outcast,” he said, according to the Washington Examiner.
West continued: "Do you want to see the underwater place?" and he claimed "I'd wear the cloak from Superman because that means you can't tell me what I have to do. Do you want the world to move forward?
Experience love.”
His comments spawned whistling at least twice from the audience and members of the NHL cast seemed embarrassed, Variety said, with a person recounting to the periodical: "A deadly silence descended on the study."
West had been invited as a last-minute replacement for singer Ariana Grande, whose ex-boyfriend rapper Mac Miller had died a few days earlier.
West baffled many with a performance from Perrier's bottle-drawn song I Love it.
