Twenty percent of students said they’re managing a “major” account cleaned up to show to parents, while maintaining a private one.
A mother who accidentally uncovered her 13-year-old daughter's secrect site found a teenager urging others to "rape me."
The research, from Digital Awareness UK and the Headmasters” and Headmistresses Conference (HMC) of private schools, showed that 40 percent of 11- to 18-year-olds own two profiles, and half of them admitted to keeping private accounts.
HMC director Mike Buchanan said: “It’s alarming that so many teenagers are tempted to create online spaces where parents and teachers can’t find them.”
