Moualem, which also serves as deputy prime minister, said that foreign forces occupy Syrian soil illegally under the pretext of fighting terrorism and "will be treated accordingly."
"They have to retire immediately without placing any conditions," he claimed before the assembly.
Moualem insisted that the "war on terrorism is almost over" in Syria, where since 2011 there have been more than 360,000 deaths and millions of people have had to leave their homes.
