The agreement between Russia and Turkey has avoided an extensive attack by Russian-backed Syrian forces in the province, where three million people live.
Moualem however stressed that the agreement has "precise deadlines" and expressed the hope that military action will target the jihadists, including the al-Nusra Front fighters linked to Al-Qaeda, which "will be eradicated."
U.N. envoy Staffan de Mistura hopes he can convene a new committee of members of the government and the opposition soon to roll out a draft constitution for post-war Syria and pave the way for elections.
Moualem laid out the conditions for participation of the Syrian government in the committee stating that the work of the group must be limited to the "revision of the articles of the current constitution" without any interference.
