A bad example of body language
At a rally held Saturday, President Donald Trump mocked Senator Dianne Feinstein for her insistence that she didn't reveal the contents of Christine Blasey Ford's letter accusing Supreme Court nominee Brett Kavanaugh of attempted rape.
During a rally in West Virginia, the president didn't talk directly about Ford's testimony before the Senate Judiciary Committee, but commented that what's going on in the Senate shows that people are "petty, bad and lying."
